# A step of for-in compares the object's structure and the order of its fields with what the list of names was made for, and loads the next name from that list.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[structure]] = Load(b@[[point]], ControlDependent|Reads:JSCell_structureID, {{*}}:ForInStep)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[names]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = 8, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:JSPropertyNameEnumerator_cachedPropertyNamesVector, {{*}}:ForInStep)
# LOOP: Int64 b@{{*}} = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:JSPropertyNameEnumerator_cachedPropertyNamesVectorContents, {{*}}:ForInStep)
# The read under that name is a call into the run time with the object and the name, and its answer comes back boxed.
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[value]] = Patchpoint(b@[[point]]:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:ElemGet)
# LOOP: Int32 b@{{*}} = AboveEqual(b@[[value]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# That read and the poll are all that can leave the loop sideways.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# CALLS: isLoopPoll, ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS: ExitsSideways{{*}}:ElemGet)
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# The counts hold calls, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 29, patchpoints: 3
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 35, patchpoints: 5
